      "title": "9.8.3 Salts of weak acids and strong bases (weak acids aur strong bases ke salts) (Roman Urdu)",
      "language": "roman_ur",
      "variant_of": "C11-CHEM-CH9-9.8.3",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 205,
          "pdf_to": 205,
          "note": "Roman Urdu explanation of topic 9.8.3, printed page 205."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Weak acid aur strong base se bane salt ki example sodium acetate hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3COONa_{(s)} + H2O_{(l)} <=> CH3COO^-_{(aq)} + Na^+_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃COONa(s) + H₂O(l) ⇌ CH₃COO⁻(aq) + Na⁺(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "CH₃COO⁻ weak acid CH₃COOH ka conjugate base hai aur pani se react karta hai:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3COO^-_{(aq)} + H2O_{(l)} <=> CH3COOH_{(aq)} + OH^-_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃COO⁻(aq) + H₂O(l) ⇌ CH₃COOH(aq) + OH⁻(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Na⁺ strong base NaOH ka conjugate acid hai aur pH par asar nahi karta. CH₃COO⁻ ion ki wajah se OH⁻ banta hai aur solution basic ho jata hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Pani mein CH₃COONa",
            "header": [
              "Ion",
              "Kis ka conjugate",
              "Pani se reaction",
              "pH par asar"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "CH₃COO⁻",
                "CH₃COOH (weak acid)",
                "CH₃COO⁻ + H₂O ⇌ CH₃COOH + OH⁻",
                "basic"
              ],
              [
                "Na⁺",
                "NaOH (strong base)",
                "koi nahi",
                "koi nahi"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "tip",
            "title": "Asaan alfaaz mein",
            "text": "Weak acid ka conjugate base pani se H⁺ “chheen” leta hai, is liye pani mein OH⁻ bach jata hai aur solution basic ho jata hai. Isi wajah se K₂CO₃ ka solution bhi basic hai (Quick Check 9.5d)."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Summary (khulasa)"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Weak acid + strong base ka salt (CH₃COONa): CH₃COO⁻ hydrolyse ho kar CH₃COOH + OH⁻ deta hai, Na⁺ nahi; solution basic."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
